# Third-party LJ artifacts, downloaded not generated -- Klein, Kraemer & Noe 2023,
# OSF https://osf.io/srqg7/. Expected at:
#     data/all_data_LJ13-1000.npy          1.5 GB, `eesi.systems.lj13.data.REF_DATA_PATH`
#     eesi/systems/lj13/LJ13_eq_OT_flow_matching 124 KB, `eesi.systems.lj13.dynamics.CKPT_PATH`
#     eesi/systems/lj13/LJ55_eq_OT_flow_matching  37 MB, the LJ55 counterpart
# The checkpoint is a bare state_dict with no extension, so *.pt does not catch it.
#
# Matched by basename, not by path: these are big binaries that must never be
# committed, and a path-anchored rule stops protecting them the moment one gets
# moved somewhere else in the tree.
all_data_LJ13-1000.npy
all_data_LJ55-1000-part1.npy
LJ13_eq_OT_flow_matching
LJ55_eq_OT_flow_matching

# TAP reference trajectories, generated externally by the active-polymer BD code.
# Same reasoning as above -- large binaries, reproducible from the generator, never
# committed. Matched by basename so a copy elsewhere in the tree stays covered.
# (The tracked xy_*.npy arrays are small derived results and are deliberately not
# caught by this pattern.)
tap_*.npy
